cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "MutCert: a transparent, parameter-free graph estimator for protein stability changes (ΔΔG)"
abstract: >-
  MutCert predicts protein stability changes (ΔΔG) for single-point mutations by
  loading a protein structure as a residue contact graph and propagating
  Miyazawa-Jernigan pairwise contact energies outward from the mutation site via
  breadth-first search with distance decay. It uses zero learned parameters and
  zero force-field hand-tuning. Its distinguishing contribution is auditability:
  a running convergence interval and a complete, inspectable per-step causal
  trace. The convergence certificate it emits attests to numerical convergence of
  the energy sum, not to the accuracy of the prediction.
